flowchart TB
  accTitle: DorkOS systems and deployment boundaries
  accDescr: The app reaches the local server. The space server is a second entry and image target of the same server package, with its own Postgres and sign-in. Cloud space management uses a separate public contract; rollout is independent of local implementation. Marketplace discovery and installation use the same package sources. The hub and agent-computer roles of the same program are omitted here; see the roles view.

  client["<b>DorkOS app</b><br/><span class='d'>Browser · phone · desktop</span>"]
  server["<b>DorkOS server</b><br/><span class='d'>Your computer's role · chats, rooms, tasks, beats, audit<br/>SQLite and files</span>"]
  runtime["<b>Agent runtimes</b><br/><span class='d'>Claude Code · Codex · OpenCode · Doe<br/>Each keeps its own history</span>"]
  cloud["<b>DorkOS Cloud · optional</b><br/><span class='d'>Accounts · managed services · credits</span>"]
  community["<b>Space server</b><br/><span class='d'>Same package, own entry and image<br/>Server sign-in · Postgres · agents are members</span>"]
  communityUI["<b>Space website</b><br/><span class='d'>The space server's own pages</span>"]
  sources["<b>Marketplace sources</b><br/><span class='d'>Registries and package repositories</span>"]
  site["<b>dorkos.ai</b><br/><span class='d'>Docs · marketplace discovery</span>"]

  client <-->|"HTTP, WebSocket<br/><span class='d'>space updates over SSE</span>"| server
  server -->|"SDK, sidecar or in process"| runtime
  server -->|"optional HTTPS"| cloud
  server <-->|"pairing · HTTP and SSE<br/><span class='d'>availability report</span>"| community
  cloud -.->|"space management<br/><span class='d'>contract only</span>"| community
  communityUI <-->|"HTTP, SSE"| community
  server -->|"fetches packages"| sources
  site -->|"reads metadata"| sources

  classDef cloud fill:#fff5e4,stroke:#a87720,color:#49320c
  classDef external fill:#ffffff,stroke:#8a9bab,color:#3b4a58
  class cloud cloud
  class sources external
